    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 257,
        "text": "Good morning, everyone. Thanks for coming to this cross-disciplinary seminar. Today we’re looking at the community garden project and how different departments collected evidence. Let’s start with you, Leo. You were in charge of the soil tests, right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "365c0347a38dd3cdf83a7b086d1181fd7688eceb2377e38d5859a9dcf2b1fc7e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 263,
        "sourceEnd": 524,
        "text": "Yes, that’s right. We took soil samples from three areas: the north bed, the south bed, and the new east bed. The north and south beds had good pH levels, around 6.5. But the east bed was more acidic, about 5.8. We think that’s because of the pine trees nearby.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a7fa4e6422db22e590dc3d691726bc1993eeaec05d56c9e2dd789583f931de70",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 531,
        "sourceEnd": 654,
        "text": "Interesting. So the east bed needs treatment before planting. Now, Priya, you looked at the water usage. What did you find?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "0a9d29c1aa87351a0bb2795b9c0f4bc24d94714b2ff1bcc868032da06d1294a2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 662,
        "sourceEnd": 935,
        "text": "Well, we measured water consumption over eight weeks. The drip irrigation system used about 30% less water than the sprinkler system. But we also noticed that the sprinkler system lost more water to evaporation, especially on hot days. So the drip system is more efficient.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "bcaa78c10cf240b0bb7608b0e01db92edd4ec2d1784556eaa332cdd10796afaf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 942,
        "sourceEnd": 990,
        "text": "Good. And what about the plant growth data, Sam?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3b82b792b616c4d05ab0dec39283ffccc1ed6cd6966b2c4a3cc5acca8a990ee8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "sam",
        "speaker": "Sam",
        "sourceStart": 996,
        "sourceEnd": 1316,
        "text": "I compared two types of tomatoes: cherry and beefsteak. The cherry tomatoes grew faster in the first month, but the beefsteak tomatoes produced more fruit by the end of the season. However, we had a problem with pests in the south bed, which affected the beefsteak plants. So the yield data might be lower than expected.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d6d25f831845812478ac25889cecf5167078f99501404021ba97c86201bc5e4e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1323,
        "sourceEnd": 1454,
        "text": "Thanks, Sam. That’s an important point about pests. Now, Chen, you interviewed the volunteers. What did they say about the project?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5afd0e529f28d605be120ec1808735e500b90e7f6f4c5aed82b500f3987bfcef",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "chen",
        "speaker": "Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1461,
        "sourceEnd": 1719,
        "text": "Most volunteers said they enjoyed working in the garden, but some mentioned that the tools were often missing or broken. Also, a few volunteers felt that the training session at the beginning was too short. They wanted more guidance on planting and watering.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a791c31d10b597dc02298c118358b8dbbce9fd9ee742d0060789022d9d6d50c1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1726,
        "sourceEnd": 1853,
        "text": "So we have some operational issues to address. Let’s move on to the budget. Hana, you reviewed the finances. Can you summarize?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "bf68832105fd8220a7999a00880c14f6ee220d6c2fcfecbe4030f6954545cf0d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "hana",
        "speaker": "Hana",
        "sourceStart": 1860,
        "sourceEnd": 2137,
        "text": "Sure. The total budget for the project was $5,000. We spent $2,000 on seeds and plants, $1,500 on tools and equipment, and $800 on water bills. The remaining $700 was used for unexpected repairs to the fence. So we stayed within budget, but there’s little left for next season.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "4a85aca221c44aeaa2fe9bdb4f16b943ab8b5eb5fc120d8e95a006bcc6be6461",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2144,
        "sourceEnd": 2292,
        "text": "Good to know. Now, let’s think about how to integrate these findings. Leo, you mentioned the soil pH. How does that relate to the plant growth data?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "29b9e71f4ffcca43bfecb5a5ad1871332d3d609b79487cbb0d1d597be56e88ea",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2298,
        "sourceEnd": 2622,
        "text": "Well, the east bed’s low pH might explain why the plants there grew more slowly. But we didn’t plant tomatoes in the east bed this season, so we can’t directly compare. However, the north and south beds had similar pH, yet the south bed had pest problems, which affected yield. So soil pH alone doesn’t tell the whole story.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "00fe11a08e757e82634e4ce0df864f4a201c1617bc490fdf02cdad48e4908938",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2629,
        "sourceEnd": 2694,
        "text": "Exactly. And Priya, how does water usage connect to plant growth?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "e38fd0714cf4addc7bee3f01510953e798421216d0be12173dc049e476095a8e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2702,
        "sourceEnd": 2917,
        "text": "The drip system was used mainly in the north bed, and that bed had good growth. But the south bed also used drip irrigation and had pest issues. So water efficiency is important, but pests can override that benefit.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "4404931de9c1ebc02b161f138981fb2c4334e383f7e593b8d5ea4778cc521859",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2924,
        "sourceEnd": 3047,
        "text": "So we need to consider multiple factors together. Chen, did the volunteers’ feedback mention anything about pests or water?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a58cbbc65cf4f7f4e834b3b4c0e82ff68499183ffec2cf6604f17200c4ca22c2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "chen",
        "speaker": "Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3054,
        "sourceEnd": 3279,
        "text": "Not directly. But some volunteers said they had trouble knowing when to water, which might relate to the training. And a few mentioned seeing insects on the plants but didn’t report them because they weren’t sure who to tell.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "8f45ba94920628ef09683e3096b4b97cca0489bba17008922c38927ffaa74a92",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3286,
        "sourceEnd": 3360,
        "text": "That’s a key gap in communication. Sam, any final thoughts from your side?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "8b903515c3627e06c958bea9b75dea3f879b8402c520a628542e6f37e0cd86d4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "sam",
        "speaker": "Sam",
        "sourceStart": 3366,
        "sourceEnd": 3613,
        "text": "Yes, I think we should repeat the experiment next season with better pest control and maybe test different tomato varieties in the east bed after adjusting the soil. Also, we should document everything more carefully so we can compare across beds.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "824ebe6580097677e3efc723f2980163f53551d6b6f9f9ff86ed9fe62cde8bdb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3620,
        "sourceEnd": 3873,
        "text": "Great. So to sum up, we have evidence from soil, water, plant growth, volunteer feedback, and budget. Each piece adds something, but no single piece gives the full picture. Our next step is to design a more integrated study for next year. Thank you all.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d4fefb660c390f4ea2e2aad3e8f609e915a5d45db53b30a970ce6d1c7fe45ec9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
